    "rich_text_ram6gnb2_intro": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_ram6gnb2_intro": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<strong>Carry More, Tow Better: NB2 GVM Upgrades for Your RAM 2500HD 6th Gen</strong>",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "enable_highlight_text_color": true,
            "heading_size": "h1",
            "heading_color": "#56bdc2"
          }
        },
        "text_ram6gnb2_intro": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h2><strong>Up to 5890 KG GVM and 2120 KG of Payload, Fully Engineered</strong></h2><p>The RAM 2500HD 6th Gen is a powerhouse from the factory, but a tray, a canopy, long range tanks and a loaded trailer will find the limit of its factory 4495 KG GVM quickly. An ORI NB2 GVM upgrade moves that limit.</p><p>Offroad Industries is a Federally Approved <strong>Second Stage Manufacturer (SSM)</strong>. These packages take GVM to <strong>5500 KG on Stage 1 and 5890 KG from Stage 2</strong>, lifting payload from 886 KG to as much as <strong>2120 KG</strong> - an increase of up to 139 per cent - with the full 4500 KG braked towing capacity left intact.</p><h3><strong>NB2 Means a Truck Licence</strong></h3><p>Because these upgrades take the vehicle above 4.5 tonnes, the RAM is reclassified into the <strong>NB2</strong> category and a light rigid truck licence is required to drive it. That is the trade for the payload.</p><p>Want the lift and the tyres without changing licence class? Our NB1 SSM packages hold GVM at 4495 KG and stay on a car licence. Talk to our team about which way suits you.</p><p>These packages are going through federal approval with a view to being approved September 2026, and apply to RAM Australia delivered vehicles.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
