    "collapsible_tabs_ram6gnb2": {
      "type": "collapsible-tabs",
      "blocks": {
        "content_ram6gnb2_1": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "RAM 2500HD 6th Gen NB2 GVM Upgrades — Carry More, Tow Better, Go Further",
            "content": "<p>The RAM 2500HD 6th Gen is one of the most capable heavy duty utes delivered in Australia, but its factory 4495 KG GVM still limits what you can legally carry once you are fully kitted out with a loaded tray, a canopy and a trailer behind you.</p><p>An ORI NB2 GVM upgrade is not a number change on paper. It is a complete engineering solution that takes GVM to 5500 KG on Stage 1 and 5890 KG from Stage 2, with the suspension components to carry it and the certification to make it legal.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "content_ram6gnb2_2": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "NB2 and Your Licence — What Changes",
            "content": "<p>Every stage here takes the vehicle above 4.5 tonnes, which moves it out of the NB1 category and into <strong>NB2</strong>. That means a light rigid truck licence is required to drive it, and it is the one real trade-off of the programme.</p><p>If you want the lift and the tyre size but not the licence change, our NB1 SSM packages for the same vehicle hold GVM at the factory 4495 KG and stay on a car licence, at the cost of the extra payload. Our team can walk you through which side of that line suits what you actually carry.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "content_ram6gnb2_3": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "How to Choose Your Stage",
            "content": "<p>Stages 1 and 2 are both a two inch lift on 35 inch tyres, so the choice is payload and suspension: Stage 1 gives 5500 KG GVM on Fox 2.5 HTO shocks, Stage 2 gives the full 5890 KG and 2120 KG of payload on Fox 2.5 Performance Elite reservoir shocks with ORI load rated coils.</p><p>Stage 3 is the first stage to clear a 37 inch tyre, with a three inch lift and a BDS radius arm kit correcting the front geometry. Stage 4 takes that to four inches and swaps the rear coils for Logic IQ air bags. Stages 5 and 6 move to the six inch platform, with Stage 6 on Fox coil-overs and clearing a 40 inch tyre.</p><p>Stages 1 to 3 are available Pre and Post Rego. Stages 4, 5 and 6 are Pre Rego only. Not sure which suits you? Contact our GVM experts.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "content_ram6gnb2_4": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Compliance, Insurance and Registration",
            "content": "<p>Offroad Industries is a Federally Approved Second Stage Manufacturer, so these upgrades are recorded on the federal database rather than signed off as one-off modifications. That is what makes them legal in every state and territory without separate engineering in each one.</p><p>Every package is engineered to the Australian Design Rules and comes with its documentation, so your insurance and warranty position is clear and on paper. We handle the certification. Remember that an NB2 vehicle needs a light rigid truck licence, so factor that in before you book.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "content_ram6gnb2_5": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Why ORI for Your RAM 2500HD 6th Gen GVM Upgrade",
